# Reopen-blank fix — NEW architecture (server-owned buffer)

> The shipped design. Aligned with moving the terminal process to a separate server.

## Idea in one line
The **server** (where the PTY lives) saves the session's **real output buffer** to disk on hibernate and replays it on reopen. The **client just renders bytes** — it has no idea hibernation happened.

## Where the "last screen" lives — on the SERVER, next to the PTY

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph CLIENT["CLIENT (renderer) — thin"]
    XT["xterm<br/>renders bytes only"]
  end
  subgraph SERVER["MAIN → standalone TERMINAL SERVER"]
    direction TB
    PTY["PTY"] --> RB["RingBuffer<br/>(live output)"]
    RB -->|"persist on hibernate"| DISK["disk<br/>terminal-buffers/"]
    DISK -->|"rehydrate on reopen"| RB
    AD["adapters: inject reset<br/>before reprint"] -.-> RB
  end
  SERVER -->|"getBufferSince replay<br/>(existing channel)"| CLIENT
  classDef good fill:#1f3d2b,stroke:#46c07a,color:#cdfadd;
  class DISK,RB good
```

Session **and** its history live together, on the server. The client holds no session state.

## Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant U as User
  participant C as Client (xterm)
  participant S as Server (PTY)
  participant D as Disk
  rect rgb(36,44,38)
  note over C,S: Hibernate
  S->>D: persist RingBuffer → file
  S->>S: kill PTY (free memory)
  end
  rect rgb(36,44,38)
  note over C,S: Reopen
  U->>C: click Reopen
  C->>S: create (resume)
  S->>D: load buffer
  D-->>S: rehydrate RingBuffer + arm reset
  S->>S: spawn CLI --resume
  C->>S: getBufferSince(-1)
  S-->>C: replay buffer (instant last screen)
  S-->>C: [reset] + reprint (live stream)
  end
```

The client runs the **same replay it already uses** for a live-PTY reattach. The reset rides the byte stream, so the client needs **no** reconcile logic.

## Why this is the robust + sustainable one
- 🟢 **State with its owner.** History lives next to the PTY → survives reconnect, second windows, web/remote clients. Rides the main→server move unchanged.
- 🟢 **Source of truth, not a copy.** Persists the real output bytes; no lossy client re-render.
- 🟢 **One source of provider knowledge.** "Reprints on resume?" stays in the server adapters.
- 🟢 **Thinner client.** All new logic is server-side; renderer reuses the replay path it already had. Main SQLite stays lean (buffers → flat file with a disk budget).

**Net:** the blank is eliminated at its root (the lost buffer is no longer lost), and every new responsibility lands on the correct side of the client/server boundary.
